          "text": "Figure 1, a horizontal stacked bar chart (in French) of mother-to-child transmission rates in the 21 Start Free, Stay Free, AIDS Free priority countries (source: UNAIDS 2018 estimates), split into transmission during the first 6 weeks and after 6 weeks. Total rates range from 26% in Indonesia (19% + 7%) and Angola (15% + 11%) down to 5% in South Africa and Botswana. The render crops the left edge, truncating some country names and the surrounding text.",
